import forgelib as F
G = F.make(slug="the-forge-forging-guide", order=12, kw="forge in the forge",
 title="How to Forge in The Forge: Masterwork and Best Katana",
 h1="How to Forge in The Forge: Better Quality, Masterwork and the Best Katana",
 desc="How to forge in The Forge for better results: ore counts, Lock Forge, molds, the Masterwork glitch from Fridge's Short, and the full recipe for the best katana.",
 kw2=["the forge masterwork","the forge best katana","the forge perfect forge","the forge lock forge","the forge weapon recipes"],
 related=["the-forge-armor-guide","the-forge-runes-guide","the-forge-heavenly-pickaxe","the-forge-volcanic-depths"],
 ids=["SCgecwSY5yY","UR3EydGUBWo"],
 lead="Every weapon and armor piece comes from the anvil, so learning how to <strong>forge in The Forge</strong> well pays off fast. Fridge has a Short on getting a \"perfect forge every time\" and a full video on the best katana. Here's how forging works today and the current katana numbers.",
 heading="Watch Fridge's Forging Videos",
 sections=[
 ("basics","How Forging Works","""<p>According to the Forge Wiki, the <strong>number of ores</strong> you put in decides your chance at each weapon type. The <strong>ores you choose</strong> decide the item's look, traits and power. Each item's multiplier is based on the ores' multipliers, so higher-multiplier ores make stronger, more valuable gear. Every recipe page lists three amounts:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Minimum ores:</strong> the base outcome chance.</li><li><strong>Recommended ores:</strong> the best outcome chance.</li><li><strong>Lock Forge:</strong> enough ores to <em>guarantee</em> that category. This was added in version 1.05 on January 18, 2026.</li></ul>
<p>Once you know these three numbers, you can forge in The Forge with a plan instead of guessing.</p>
<p>Molds, added in version 1.08 on September 5, 2026, boost the odds further. Weapon Molds drop from the Reaper (1 in 32), Cthulhu (1 in 8) and Asura's Incarnate (1 in 18), and enough of them can give a 100% chance for select weapons.</p>"""),
 ("masterwork","Masterwork and the \"Perfect Forge\" Short","""<p>Fridge's December 22, 2025 Short shows a glitch for getting a top-quality, Masterwork forge every time. Treat it as a snapshot: glitches like this are usually patched, and the game has had several forging updates since. The legitimate ways to raise forge quality now are:</p>
<ul><li>Use the <strong>recommended</strong> ore count, or the Lock Forge count, instead of the minimum.</li><li>The <strong>Dwarf</strong> race gives +5% Better Forge.</li><li>The <strong>Better Forge</strong> gamepass (449 Robux) increases forge quality. <strong>Fast Forge</strong> (299 Robux) makes forging faster, and the wiki says it skips the forging minigames.</li><li>Forge during the <strong>Forge Fever</strong> world event.</li></ul>
<p>\"Masterwork\" is also the name of a monthly Questboard quest: enhance any item to +6 or +7 for Gold and XP.</p>"""),
 ("katana","The Best Katana in The Forge","""<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Katanas (Forge Wiki, November 11, 2026)</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Katana</th><th scope="col">Base damage</th><th scope="col">Attack speed</th><th scope="col">Unlock</th><th scope="col">Chance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Straight Edge Katana</td><td>9.35</td><td>0.69s</td><td>Fungi Shop blueprint; forge on the Forgotten Kingdom or Crimson Sakura</td><td>1/6</td></tr>
<tr><td>Juto Katana</td><td>8.5</td><td>0.69s</td><td>Level 102; Crimson Sakura</td><td>1/2</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Both katanas use <strong>9 minimum ores, 12 recommended and 18 to Lock Forge</strong>, with a 9.45-stud range. The <strong>Straight Edge Katana</strong> has the higher base damage. Its blueprint comes from <strong>Fungi</strong>, who sells weapon blueprints in the heart of the Secret Maze on Island 3 (see our <a href="the-forge-heavenly-pickaxe.html">Maze guide</a>). Fridge's video came out on December 19, 2025, before the Maze existed, so how you unlock it has changed since.</p>"""),
 ("ores","Which Ores to Use","""<p>The ores matter as much as the count when you forge in The Forge. The wiki's weapon guide works in ore ratios for straight swords, the closest type to katanas. On the Forgotten Kingdom, the endgame mix is <strong>4 Darkryte + 2 Magmaite</strong>, and Eye Ore + Rivalite works for midgame. On the Frostspire Expanse, endgame is <strong>2 Gargantuan + 2 Golem Heart + 2 Voidstar</strong>. Scale those ratios up to the katana's 12 recommended ores. Get the ores from our <a href="the-forge-volcanic-depths.html">Volcanic Depths guide</a>, and add weapon runes with the <a href="the-forge-runes-guide.html">runes guide</a>.</p>""")],
 faq=[("How do you get better forges in The Forge?","Use the recommended or Lock Forge ore count, use high-multiplier ores, and add molds. The Dwarf race and the Better Forge gamepass also raise quality."),
      ("What is the best katana in The Forge?","The Straight Edge Katana, with 9.35 base damage. Its blueprint is sold by Fungi in the Secret Maze."),
      ("Does the Masterwork glitch still work in The Forge?","Probably not. It's from December 2025, and the game has had several forging updates since.")],
 sources=[F.wiki("Weapons"),F.wiki("Straight_Edge_Katana","Straight Edge Katana"),F.wiki("Juto_Katana","Juto Katana"),F.wiki("Weapon_Mold","Weapon Mold"),F.wiki("Gamepass","Gamepasses"),F.wiki("Masterwork","Masterwork quest"),F.wiki("Guide","Community guide: weapon recipes"),F.wiki("Version_History","Version History")])
